// PHASE 6 - PAGE 31: DARK EMOTIONS - INTRO
// Shadow Work Philosopher: 200+ words on taboo emotions and somatic expression
// Mirroring technique included

#somatic_page(
  title: "Phase 6: Dark Emotions – Rage, Envy & Shame",
  body_text: [
    #align(center)[
      _"The cure for the pain is in the pain."_
      
      — Rumi
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    You may notice a clenching in your jaw as you read these forbidden words—rage, envy, shame. Perhaps heat rises in your face, or your belly tightens with ancient disgust. The body braces against the mere *naming* of what has been banished. *This contraction is your shadow, asking to finally be witnessed.*
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #rect(fill: rgb("#F5F5F0"), stroke: 0.5pt + gray, inset: 15pt, radius: 2pt)[
      Some emotions are so taboo that we bury them immediately. Rage. Envy. Hatred. Shame. We were taught that "good people" do not feel these things, so we exiled them to the darkest corners of the psyche. But Jung was clear: *what we resist persists, and what we deny runs our lives from the shadows.*
      
      These emotions do not disappear when suppressed—they transmute. Repressed rage becomes depression (anger turned inward), chronic muscle tension, autoimmune disorders, or explosive outbursts that terrify us. Unexpressed envy poisons our relationships with bitterness and passive-aggression. Unmetabolized shame corrodes self-worth from the inside, manifesting as perfectionism, people-pleasing, or self-destruction.
      
      Somatic psychology reveals that emotions are fundamentally *physical events*—waves of energy designed to move through the body and then discharge. But when we suppress this movement, the energy becomes trapped, crystallizing into chronic holding patterns. Rage lives in the jaw, the fists, the legs (the urge to kick). Shame curls in the belly and collapses the chest. Envy coils around the heart like thorned vines.
      
      The only way out is *through*—but through safely, with ritual containment. We give these dark emotions permission to *move* so they can finally release their grip on our bodies and our lives.
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    *In this phase, you will:*
    - Give voice to your forbidden emotions through safe somatic expression
    - Express rage through the body using the Rage Release ritual
    - Map where dark emotions live in your physical tissue
    - Transform shame into self-compassion through embodied practice
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
